.th GPROCS II
.sh NAME
gprocs \*- get system process information
.sh SYNOPSIS
(gprocs = 61.; not in assembler)
.br
(buf in r0)
.br
.ft B
sys gprocs
.br
.ft R
(number of process slots in r0)
.s3
.ft B
gprocs(buf);
.br
char *buf;
.ft R
.sh DESCRIPTION
.bd Gprocs
returns a copy of the system
process table in the users area
.it buf.
.it Buf
must be large enough to accomodate the whole of this information.
.bd Gprocs
returns a word (in r0) containing the number of process slots in
the system.
.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 20
/usr/sys/param.h	for number of processes
/usr/sys/proc.h	for process structure
.fi
.sh "SEE ALSO"
skill (I), skill (III), alive (III)
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
Error bit (c-bit) is set for segmentation violations.
From C, a -1 value is returned on error.
